  <title id="bdl27trainingprocedures-title">Training procedures of ADKF-IFT, DKT and DKL</title>
  <desc id="bdl27trainingprocedures-desc">Panel a, ADKF-IFT: three tasks T1, T2 and T3 pass through one shared feature extractor whose parameters psi meta equal phi. Each task gets its own GP; its base kernel parameters psi adapt are optimized on that task's train loss, giving three differently adapted GP posteriors that feed an expected validation loss, and psi meta is updated using the implicit function theorem. Panel b, DKT: the three tasks share one feature extractor and one GP with psi meta equal to theta and phi; all parameters are optimized on the expected validation loss. Panel c, DKL: each task has its own network and GP, with psi adapt equal to theta and phi, optimized on that task's own train loss.</desc>
